.TH BUILDABOOK 1 "October 2026" "buildabook 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
buildabook \- build a typeset book from a plain-text outline
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buildabook
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B buildabook spine
.I file.pdf
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buildabook
turns a plain-text outline into a typeset book.  One outline file drives the
chapter numbering, the table of contents, and every cross-reference, so the
book is a build artifact of a single source of order.
.PP
The program reads
.IR outline.txt ,
the one source of sequence and numbering, resolves
.B {{token}}
cross-references in the chapter source files, and writes a Typst
.I book.typ
together with a
.I number_map.csv
audit.
.PP
The point of the tool is that a writer, human or LLM, never writes a number or
a page reference by hand.  The prose holds stable tokens such as
.BR {{c:00042}} ;
buildabook computes the number at build time from the outline's row order, and
page references resolve through native Typst lookups.  Inserting, deleting, or
reordering a chapter is one line in the outline; every reference follows on
the next build.  The
.B check
subcommand catches the mistakes a prose pass cannot hold in its head, such as
duplicate UUIDs, unmatched files, and unresolvable tokens.
.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B render
Read the outline, resolve tokens, and emit the rendered Typst book and the
number map.  This is the default operation.
.TP
.B check
Validate the outline, the file map, and every token reference.  Emit nothing;
exit nonzero on the first error.
.TP
.B number-map
Write
.I number_map.csv
only.
.TP
.B spine \fIfile.pdf\fR
Rewrite the cover spine width from the page count of
.IR file.pdf ,
updating the
.B #let sw
binding in the cover template.
.TP
.B build
Convenience wrapper: render, compile the PDF with Typst, then run
.BR spine .
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-outline " file"
Outline file to read (default
.IR outline.txt ).
.TP
.BI \-\-src " dir"
Directory holding the chapter source files (default
.IR chapters ).
.TP
.BI \-\-out " dir"
Directory for the rendered output (default
.IR rendered ).
.TP
.BI \-\-number-map " file"
Where to write the CSV audit (default
.IR number_map.csv ).
.TP
.B \-\-ignore-unmatched
Do not fail when a source file's heading matches no outline token.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-table-rows " n"
Split tables longer than
.I n
rows (0 disables).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I outline.txt
The outline: one entry or directive per line, with
.B #
comments.  See
.BR LANGUAGE.md .
.TP
.I filemap.txt
Optional
.IR UUID:filename
map.  When absent, each source file is matched by its first heading.
.TP
.I book.conf
Book metadata (title, author, slug) in the OpenBSD-style configuration
language, parsed by the hbnf runtime.
.TP
.I number_map.csv
Generated audit of every UUID and its rendered designation.
.
.SH LIMITATIONS
.PP
A title or directive value runs to end of line, so it cannot contain a literal
newline, and there is no trailing-comment syntax.  Each entry is addressed by a
five-digit UUID, so a writer must look up a UUID rather than a number; the
number map is the look-up aid.  A page reference to a section requires that
section's heading to carry its token.  A
.B k:
sub-entry binds to the chapter whose UUID is its
.B NNNNN
part, which the engine does not verify at parse time.  The book is emitted as
one Typst document; splitting a book across volumes is a Makefile-level
concern, not an engine feature.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TYPST
Path to the Typst compiler, used by
.BR build .
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; nonzero if the outline, file map, or a token reference is
invalid, or if a subcommand is unknown.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
buildabook check
buildabook render --outline outline.txt --src chapters --out rendered
buildabook spine book.pdf
buildabook build
.fi
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR LANGUAGE.md ,
.BR typst (1)
.
